1
00:00:00,137 --> 00:00:03,097
(Howard:)Okay, Sheldon,
what was it supposed to be?

2
00:00:03,557 --> 00:00:06,307
(Howard:)Fine, it's out of the washer.

3
00:00:06,477 --> 00:00:08,937
(Howard:)I'll call you when it's in the dryer.

4
00:00:09,438 --> 00:00:10,438
All right, let's go.

5
00:00:10,606 --> 00:00:12,606
[CLEARING THROAT]

6
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:22,032
[PENNY SIGHING]

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,370
- What do you think?
- Um, that one.

8
00:00:25,538 --> 00:00:28,378
- Because of the additional Ethernet ports?
- Sure.

9
00:00:28,541 --> 00:00:31,211
(Sheldon:)He doesn't need them.
He's got a six-port Ethernet switch.

10
00:00:31,377 --> 00:00:33,047
- Oh, okay, then this one.
- Why?

11
00:00:33,212 --> 00:00:36,342
(Howard:)I don't know.
The man on the box looks so happy.

12
00:00:36,716 --> 00:00:39,886
Penny, if I'm going to buy Leonard a gift,
I'm going to do it right.

13
00:00:40,052 --> 00:00:43,142
(Sheldon:)I refuse to let him experience
the same childhood trauma I did.

14
00:00:43,764 --> 00:00:46,804
I know I'm gonna regret this,
but what trauma?

15
00:00:48,144 --> 00:00:51,734
On my 12th birthday,
I really wanted a titanium centrifuge...

16
00:00:51,897 --> 00:00:54,737
(Sheldon:)...so, you know,
I could separate radioactive isotopes.

17
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,030
Of course, yeah.

18
00:00:56,193 --> 00:01:00,193
(Sheldon:)Instead of a titanium centrifuge,
my parents bought me...

